Danny Boyle says he used to believe that he that he never made the same film twice, thus a filmography that includes hit movies across genres like Shallow Grave, Trainspotting, 127 Hours, The Beach, 28 Days Later and of course Slumdog Millionaire , the 2009 Best Picture Oscar winner that also won him Best Director.

But Boyle, speaking onstage Saturday after receiving the Deadline Legend Award during Deadline's Contenders Film Los Angeles awards-season event, said he was set straight on that idea long ago.

&#8220;I can't remember if it was a press conference or a Q&A in Paris, and this French journalist stood up at the back and said, &#8216;This is nonsense, Mr. Boyle',&#8221; he recalled. &#8220;And I said, &#8216;Excuse me, what?' And she said, &#8216;All your films are exactly the same.' She said, &#8216;They're all about, and it's usually a guy, who overcomes, who faces insurmountable odds and overcomes them.' And with that she walked out.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He continued, &#8220;Ever since then I've accepted that she's absolutely right &#8212; they are all about the same thing, really. And you do realize, and you can see in other filmmakers as well. You're desperately trying to make a different film, and they basically turn out the same in a way. They're the skeleton or the the kind of architecture of them is the same somehow. I have to hold my hand up and admit that. So if you keep buying tickets to go and see the films, thank you.&#8221; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Boyle's latest entry on his list is Ink , based on Hames Graham's Tony-winning play about Rupert Murdoch and editor Larry Lamb's efforts to revive the British newspaper The Sun , ushering in a new kind of tabloid journalism with lurid headlines and questionable tactics. Graham adapted the screenplay for the pic, which opened this year's Venice Film Festival and is gearing for its December 11 release in theaters.

In Ink &#8216;s case, the underdogs in question are Guy Pearce's Murdoch and Jack O'Connell's Lamb, who are faced with the daunting task to make inroads against a dozen UK paper including what Doyle called &#8220;the Real Madrid&#8221; of publications at the time, The Mirror . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;One of them from Australia, and the other one from Yorkshire in the north of England, with a plan to beat [ The Mirror ] in a year, in just one year, to overtake it in a year,&#8221; Boyle said in conversation with Deadline's Mike Fleming Jr. &#8220;And what they did in order to do that was, in my contention and James', is that they invented the tabloid vernacular, the language, the the vocabulary, the techniques of the tabloid, and they began to use it. And it connected with what people in Britain wanted, who were still in a dreary world of paternalism and postwar &#8216;we know what's best for you' kind of mentality, and they suddenly found a kind of liberation.&#8221;

That's in the first half of the film, which he said &#8220;I hope is very very funny because it employs the tabloid techniques to to gain your trust really, but through your pleasure. Then it begins to change a little bit when you find out some of the things that they're up to and some of the costs of what that approach entails.&#8221;

Boyle during the conversation also confirmed that headlines that appeared in the movie's epilogue that have been redacted in UK versions of the film because of stringent libel laws will be shown in the U.S. versions .

He also said a difference from Graham's play is Claire Foy's character Jules Davies, a composite of several women who worked at The Sun including one that had an affair with Lamb. Lamb's son objected to the inclusion, Boyle said, because he thought it disparaged the memory of his mother, &#8220;which is absolutely right,&#8221; the director says.

&#8220;The film's about Larry Lamb and his reputation and his behavior. And he was a public figure. And it's only right and proper that we have the right to investigate him,&#8221; Boyle said. &#8220;He changed British society significantly in many ways, as much as Margaret Thatcher changed British society.&#8221;

Thatcher also appears in the film. &#8220;We didn't want an impersonator to play her, so we actually re-created her, the real Margaret Thatcher. But we didn't ask Margaret Thatcher's estate because these powerful people, we have to be able to investigate them, and provided you do it truthfully and responsibly &#8230;. I think it's right to have that kind of artistic license. In fact, it's crucial to freedom and artistic freedom that you do have that license with public figures.

Boyle also provided an update on a third installment of the 28 Years Later franchise , after he and Alex Garland brought back the franchise in 2025. A second movie, Nia DaCosta's 28 Years Later: The Bone Temple also penned by Garland, hit theaters this past January.

&#8220;Alex has written a fantastic script. Seriously, he's written a fantastic script, so we've got to raise the money to make it,&#8221; Boyle said. He also confirmed that Cillian Murphy , who appeared in the 2002 Boyle-directed franchise starter 28 Days Later , was game to return.

&#8220;I mean, he's up for it, and it's a fantastic part &#8212; Alex has written this fantastic part for him,&#8221; Boyle said. &#8220;Those of you who saw [ Bone Temple ], he's teased at the end of that, and then the third film does complete the story in a beautiful, mathematically perfect way in which the circle is closed in a way that even Chris Nolan might admire, actually, because it's perfect. So let's hope it all comes together.&#8221;

Check back Monday for the video of the conversation.

While Elizabeth Olsen &#8216;s Wanda Maximoff makes a brief return in VisionQuest &#8216;s credits scene , there were talks about bringing her back for a bigger presence.

Paul Bettany , who reprised his role as Vision and executive produced the MCU series on Disney+, noted that he and Kevin Feige ultimately agreed the show was worth letting it &#8220;stand on its own&#8221; as opposed to distracting audiences with another big character.

&#8220;There were questions about it, whether that should happen, whether it opened up too much for the MCU, whether they wanted to do it later. I don't know,&#8221; Bettany told The Playlist . &#8220;But I remember having this conversation with [Feige], and he said, &#8216;You and Terry have done such a great job at making me care about Vision. I really don't think you should distract from that by giving the audience that at the end of the [show]. It will just fundamentally all become about WandaVision again, and this should and can stand on its own.' And I think he was right.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Although Wanda doesn't reunite with Vision or their sons in the series, the post-credits scene showed what appeared to be Doctor Doom reviving her from the rubble of Wundagore following the events of Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness (2022).

With the scene appearing to hint at her presence in Avengers: Doomsday , Bettany admitted that he &#8220;would love&#8221; to reunite with Olsen for another series in their continuity, following WandaVision (2021), Agatha All Along (2024) and VisionQuest .

&#8220;Gosh, I would love for that to be. I don't know,&#8221; he said. &#8220;I mean, at the moment, it doesn't feel that way, but I've died so many times in this show, so you never actually know.&#8221;

Bettany continued, &#8220;And my experience of Hollywood tells me if something's a big enough hit, people want to continue with that. So I mean, I guess we'll see. And whether Vision continues at all is sadly a decision that is made further up the food chain than I sit.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

After Vision was reunited with both their sons Tommy (Ruaridh Mollica) and Billy (Joe Locke) in the VisionQuest finale, it's possible we'll see a family reunion with Wanda in Avengers: Doomsday , premiering Dec. 18 in theaters.

Ink director Danny Boyle on Saturday confirmed that redacted Sun newspaper headlines shown as part of an epilogue in his Netflix drama about the founding of the UK tabloid will be shown in full in the U.S. theatrical and streaming version of the film.

Speaking while receiving the Deadline Legend Awards during Deadline's Contenders Film Los Angeles awards-season event Saturday, Boyle said an edited version showing the headlines is currently being edited into a new cut of the film in time for its December 11 release in select theaters.

The pic, based on James Graham's play and adapted screenplay that tells the story of Rupert Murdoch and editor Larry Lamb's takeover of the British tabloid The Sun in the late 1960s, setting the tone for new kind of journalism in the process, was unable to show the headlines owing to Britain's stringent libel laws. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;We've had a battle to get the film to where it is now, and I can tell you &#8212; I can say this, can't I? &#8212; I think that we just won the ability [to show the headlines] because we're in America, and you have better protection for freedom of speech than we have in Britain,&#8221; Boyle said during the Q&A session at the DGA Theater, adding that he hopes the uncensored version &#8220;will be [in] the finished version of the film, which we've never been able to show in Britain.&#8221; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Boyle pointed to one specific headline in the epilogue that was redacted in UK versions of the pic, above an article about the 1989 death of 97 fans crushed while trying to enter Hillsborough Stadium to watch a Liverpool-Nottingham Forest FA Cup soccer game. The tabloid report blamed Liverpool fans for the tragedy, citing what turned out to fabricated police and official reports.

&#8220;There are various headlines &#8230; at the end of [ Ink ], and there's one particular, which although it won't mean anything to you, to anybody from Britain it does mean a great deal, which is that The Sun ran a terrible headline called &#8216;The Truth,' which is one of the principal concerns of James Graham's screenplay throughout the whole film,&#8221; Boyle said. &#8220;[ The Sun ] ran this headline, and it was a bunch of lies about the way that Liverpool fans were killed at the Hillsborough disaster,&#8221; he continued. &#8220;It's one of the low points of British journalism, and we wanted that to be always in the film, and we weren't able to have it in the British version. We have these redacted versions, but know that we're in America. We've got it in there, and I hope that the tidal wave will then reach back to Britain, and we'll be allowed to put them in there because it's an important moment for freedom of speech, which you have enshrined.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

He added, &#8220;You know, it's it's it's interesting that a tabloid that you know that lets it all hang out would try to stop you from doing something similar.&#8221;

The epilogue in the pic, which stars Jack O'Connell as Lamb and Guy Pearce as Murdoch, is also key as it ties The Sun's rise to modern tabloids &#8212; and Murdoch's eventual founding of Fox News .

&#8220;What they ignited &#8230; and the pact that they came up with to start The Sun culminates financially and principally in the birth of Fox News,&#8221; Boyle said. &#8220;Because the money that The Sun made allowed Murdoch to buy 20th Century Fox and then to finance the establishment, the extraordinary establishment, of a new terrestrial channel in America, which takes a lot of money. So there's an umbilical cord, I think, that connects these two guys and their meeting in 1969 with where we are now.&#8221;

Ink , which has been hitting festival since its world premiere to open this year's Venice Film Festival, is due to open in the UK on January 8, when it becomes available to stream on Netflix.

Have you ever been serenaded at 35,000 feet by Hoobastank ? We're betting that answer is no.

But about 125 lucky Southwest Airline passengers got that opportunity on Friday on a charted Southwest Airlines flight from Los Angeles to headed to the Vans Warped Tour in Orlando.

The festivities actually kicked off that morning in Terminal 1 of LAX. At the gate, guests &#x2014; who were mostly dressed in black, rock-themed attire, with plenty donning sort of Vans apparel, from shoes to purses to hats &#x2014; were greeted with a rock music playlist as passengers had the opportunity to perform their favorites. (Shout-out to the woman named Gianna who gave a high-energy performance of Fall Out Boy's &#8220;Sugar, We're Goin Down.&#8221;) Then they were invited to a meet-and-greet with recording artists Lolo , Simple Plan , Hoobastank and The Used , all of whom are were on the Vans Warped Tour lineup. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies 'Fatherland' Wins Top Camerimage Prize as 'Wild Horse Nine' Nabs Audience Award TV Philomena Cunk Comes for Hollywood

What some of the passengers &#x2014; who included fans, influences and journalists &#x2014; didn't realize is that all four acts were going to perform on the flight to Orlando. The initiative is part of the airline's Live at 35, an in-flight entertainment program &#x2014; celebrating its 15th anniversary this year &#x2014; that surprises passengers with live pop-up music performances and events at 35,000 feet.

Once in the air, singer Lolo kicked things off somewhere over Texas with a four-song set. At one point, Lolo shared that she &#8220;almost didn't take the gig because I'm a nervous flier and this is the longest I've gone without wearing a seat belt.&#8221; (Incidentally, the flight took off about an hour before the Federal Aviation Administration grounded all U.S. flights &#8220;due to extraordinary circumstances and for reasons of safety.&#8221; The buzz on the plane was that our flight was likely one of very few planes in the air at the time.) blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The aforementioned Hoobastank performed a trio of sings, culminating with their 2004 smash hit &#8220;The Reason.&#8221; During that song, lead singer Doug Robb asked the flight staff to turn off all the lights and the passengers to turn on their cell flashlights, upping the concert vibe inside the aircraft. The passengers also took part in a rousing sing-along to the tune.

&#8220;Is this the most annoying flight you've ever been on?&#8221; Robb joked. Walking through the plane, he swiped an iPad from a passenger who was evidently doing some online shopping. &#8220;I think you should buy that,&#8221; he joked.

During his set, The Used frontman Bert McCracken noted the unusual &#8220;venue&#8221; as the flight was passing over New Orleans. &#8220;This is the weirdest fucking shit I've ever done in my life,&#8221; he quipped. The band played four songs, and also turned &#8220;The Taste of Ink&#8221; into a sing-along. (&#8220;Everyone knows the lyrics to this song. It's called &#8216;The Reason,'&#8221; McCracken joked in a callback to Hoobastank's crowd-participation performance.)

Simple Plan's Pierre Bouvier took the stage &#x2014; floor? aisle? &#x2014; last, performing songs including &#8220;I'd Do Anything.&#8221; After the song, he joked, &#8220;Give it up for Mark Hoppus,&#8221; the Blink-182 singer-bassist who is featured on the song. (Hoppus was not present.)

Bouvier joked it was &#8220;super awkward&#8221; to perform on a plane, even changing the lyrics to &#8220;I'd do anything for you, Vans Warped Tour,&#8221; before giving a knowing look and quipping, &#8220;Really, anything .&#8221; Bouvier also sang &#8220;I'm Just a Kid,&#8221; noting that it went viral on social media several years after its release as part of the #ImJustAKidChallenge Challenge, where users re-created childhood photographs as adults or adolescents. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

As the plane began descending, Bouvier asked the flight crew to turn down the lights, quipping that &#8220;the flight crew didn't know they were going to become the light crew.&#8221;

Markus Lloyd is the host for these events, which have featured acts including Julian Marley (son of Bob), the Plain White T's, Magic!, Shane Smith & The Saints, Barenaked Ladies, Imagine Dragons, Chris Young and Cassidy Pope. &#8220;What's fun&#8221; about these experiences, he told THR, &#8220;is that when we're heading someplace fun, like the Vans Warped Tour, or Vegas, the plane has already kind of turned up a bit. And so when you tell them they're getting this extra thing, it's like they won the lottery. They're like, &#8216;Oh my gosh, I'm going to Vegas AND I get a concert in the place? And that's when we go, &#8216;You can't get this anywhere besides Southwest.'&#8221;

For an encore on Friday's flight, Hoobastank got up to perform one last song just moments before the flight landed safely in Orlando.

Richard Sterban , the lead singer of the Oak Ridge Boys whose bass vocals brought 1981's &#8220;Elvira&#8221; cover to life, was 83.

The Country Music Hall of Famer's family and band announced that he died on Saturday in Hendersonville, Tennessee, due to complications from bronchitis and pneumonia &#8220;after fighting a long, hard battle with cancer.&#8221;

&#8220;We appreciate all of your love, support, and prayers,&#8221; Sterban's family said in a statement. &#8220;Please continue to lift us up in this difficult time, we find comfort knowing that he is currently face to face with Jesus.&#8221;

Sterban previously stepped away from touring with the Oak Ridge Boys for health reasons in May 2025, but he reunited with the group in January to sing &#8220;Elvira&#8221; at the Grand Ole Opry. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Born Richard Anthony Sterban on April 24, 1943 in Camden, New Jersey, he began singing in Sunday school and glee club before co-founding the gospel quartet Keystones. As part of JD Sumner and the Stamps Quartet, Sterban backed Elvis Presley on tour, immortalized in the 1972 concert film Elvis on Tour .

In 1972, Sterban stepped away from the King's tour to joined the Oak Ridge Boys along with lead singer Duane Allen, baritone William Lee Golden and tenor Joe Bonsall, who died at age 76 of complications with ALS in 2024. &#8220;I wanted to be in the best vocal group in the world,&#8221; he once said.

The Oak Ridge Boys, which has sold more than 41 million records, won five Grammys and was inducted into the Country Music Hall of Fame in 2015. The group was founded in 1943 as the Oak Ridge Quartet, changing its name to the Oak Ridge Boys in the 1960s as it moved from its original bluegrass sound to gospel and eventually country.

During their '81 cover of Dallas Frazier's &#8220;Elvira,&#8221; Sterban's bass vocals were used for the &#8220;oom poppa mow mow&#8221; riff. Going to No. 1 on the country chart and No. 5 on the pop chart, the track sold more than 2M copies, was named Single of the Year by both the CMA and the Academy of Country Music, and won the Grammy Award for Best Country Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocal. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The group was also known for &#8220;Bobbie Sue,&#8221; &#8220;American Made,&#8221; &#8220;Dream On,&#8221; &#8220;Gonna Take a Lot of River,&#8221; &#8220;No Matter How High,&#8221; and more during Sterban's 28-year tenure.

Sterban is survived by his wife, Donna, daughters Lauren (Tyler) and Tori (Michael), sons Rich (Chele), Doug and Chris, grandchildren Mali (Zachary), Nikolas, Tyler (Ryann), Madelyn, Alexandra, Rex, Owen and Charli Grace, and great-grandchildren Salem, Asher and Theo. He was preceded in death by mother Victoria Sterban, brother Joseph Sterban and grandson Zachary.

Broadway's The Rocky Horror Show was the setting for a Glee mini-reunion last night, as Lea Michele , Jenna Ushkowitz and Becca Tobin showed up to catch the show now starring their former castmate Kevin McHale .

In a short video clip posted on the Rocky Horror Instagram page, the four Glee stars gather backstage and lip-sync to their old show's line "You're all minorities. You're in the glee club." (Check out the video below.)

Ushkowitz posted some additional photos from the meet-up; see those below, too. &#8220;A time was had seeing @kevinmchale this weekend in his first ever Broadway show,&#8221; she wrote in the caption. &#8220;To say I'm proud would be the understatement of the century. Best weekend in the big &#x1F34E; with these hot Mamas who deserved a little R & R.&#8221; The get-together arrived amidst lots of online chatter about the possibility of the original gang's participation in Ryan Murphy's Glee reboot ordered to series by Disney+ and Hulu last month. Murphy has said that as many as 10 original cast members have been approached to participate. Chris Colfer, who played Kurt Hummel on the original Fox series, said recently he's had a &#8220;nice conversation&#8221; about his potential return. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Chris Colfer In "Conversation" About 'Glee' Reboot, Jokes He'll Return If Mr. Schue & Sue Perform "WAP" News Harry Shum Jr. On Reprising Roles In 'Glee' Revival & 'Crazy Rich Asians' Series: "Would Love To Try & Find A Way To Make It Work"

